<Ui>
    <!--
        The cinematic frame — what makes InCinematic() true, and the ESC that skips a fly-by.
        Transcribed from the reference's Interface\FrameXML\CinematicFrame.xml + .lua (decision
        1602 permits it); the engine half is crate::cinematic.

        This frame is load-bearing for exactly one thing, and it is not a picture: it is the WHOLE
        skip path. In the reference, StopCinematic (0x48b970) has zero native callers and no
        Bindings.xml row — the only thing that ever calls it is the OnKeyDown below, reached
        because this fullscreen frame is keyboard-enabled and showing. No frame on screen means no
        way out of a 102-second Night Elf intro.

        THE BLACK BARS ARE NOT HERE, deliberately. The reference draws them as two textures on this
        frame; we draw them as Bevy UI nodes in crate::cinematic instead, because a cinematic hides
        the HUD through UiHidden — which kills both of ui_pass's quad lanes wholesale, and the
        FrameXML layer is one of them. Bars declared here would go dark along with the action bars
        they exist to replace. The bar LAW is unchanged and still the reference's — but it is BOTH
        halves of it (decision 1701): the Lua's `if width/height > 4/3` guards a *recompute*, not
        whether there are bars, and below it the XML's own `1024x128` textures stand on the native
        1024x768 sheet, i.e. height/6 — which is the 2:1 crop evaluated at exactly 4:3. One
        expression covers both: `min((h - min(w/2, h))/2, h/6)`. See `drive_letterbox`.

        So this frame draws nothing at all. It is kept rather than replaced with an engine-side key
        handler because the skip path IS a frame in the reference: keeping it means ESC works for
        the same reason it works there, and an addon that hooks CinematicFrame still finds it.

        RunBinding("SCREENSHOT") is kept as the reference has it: while this frame eats the
        keyboard, the screenshot key is the one binding that still has to get through.
    -->
    <Script><![CDATA[
        function CinematicFrame_OnLoad()
            this:RegisterEvent("CINEMATIC_START");
            this:RegisterEvent("CINEMATIC_STOP");
        end

        function CinematicFrame_OnEvent()
            if ( event == "CINEMATIC_START" ) then
                ShowUIPanel(this, 1);
                return;
            end
            if ( event == "CINEMATIC_STOP" ) then
                HideUIPanel(this);
                return;
            end
        end
    ]]></Script>
    <Frame name="CinematicFrame" setAllPoints="true" hidden="true" enableKeyboard="true" enableMouse="true">
        <Scripts>
            <OnLoad>
                CinematicFrame_OnLoad();
            </OnLoad>
            <OnEvent>
                CinematicFrame_OnEvent();
            </OnEvent>
            <OnKeyDown>
                local screenshotKey = GetBindingKey("SCREENSHOT");
                if ( arg1 == "ESCAPE" ) then
                    StopCinematic();
                elseif ( screenshotKey and (arg1 == screenshotKey) ) then
                    RunBinding("SCREENSHOT");
                end
            </OnKeyDown>
        </Scripts>
    </Frame>
</Ui>
